//!
//! ## Constructing Tree Views
//!
//! When using the `--tree` argument, instead of a vector of cells, each row
//! has a `depth` field that indicates how far deep in the tree it is: the top
//! level has depth 0, its children have depth 1, and *their* children have
//! depth 2, and so on.
//!
//! On top of this, it also has a `last` field that specifies whether this is
//! the last row of this particular consecutive set of rows. This doesn鈥檛
//! affect the file鈥檚 information; it鈥檚 just used to display a different set of
//! Unicode tree characters! The resulting table looks like this:
//!
//! ```text
//!     鈹屸攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹?
//!     鈹?Depth 鈹?Last  鈹?Output                鈹?
//!     鈹溾攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹尖攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹尖攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹?
//!     鈹?    0 鈹?      鈹?documents             鈹?
//!     鈹?    1 鈹?false 鈹?鈹溾攢鈹€ this_file.txt     鈹?
//!     鈹?    1 鈹?false 鈹?鈹溾攢鈹€ that_file.txt     鈹?
//!     鈹?    1 鈹?false 鈹?鈹溾攢鈹€ features          鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?false 鈹?鈹?  鈹溾攢鈹€ feature_1.rs  鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?false 鈹?鈹?  鈹溾攢鈹€ feature_2.rs  鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?true  鈹?鈹?  鈹斺攢鈹€ feature_3.rs  鈹?
//!     鈹?    1 鈹?true  鈹?鈹斺攢鈹€ pictures          鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?false 鈹?    鈹溾攢鈹€ garden.jpg    鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?false 鈹?    鈹溾攢鈹€ flowers.jpg   鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?false 鈹?    鈹溾攢鈹€ library.png   鈹?
//!     鈹?    2 鈹?true  鈹?    鈹斺攢鈹€ space.tiff    鈹?
//!     鈹斺攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹粹攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹粹攢鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹€鈹?
